<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adityawarman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1375</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adityawarman was a Sumatran king of Malayu and Javanese descent who had served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> before founding his own kingdom in the Minangkabau highlands. In 1347 he inscribed the back of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amoghapasa">Amoghapasa</a> statue of Dharmasraya, declaring himself king, and he later ruled from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagaruyung">Pagaruyung</a> region. His many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> inscriptions are the main sources for 14th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adityawarman.jpg" alt="Adityawarman" width="320" height="581" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lehmkuhl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adityawarman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
